in a shanghai supermarket two men get  into a fight while shopping for last  minute supplies  tensions are high since the announcement  of a phased corvette 19 lockdown  the first ever imposed in the chinese  commercial center  from monday those living in the eastern  and southern parts of the city are being  forced to stay home  public transport has been suspended and  mass testing has begun  the lockdown will be lifted on friday  when the same restrictions will be  applied to the other half of the city  earlier this month authorities reassured  the public there would be no mass  shutdown in shanghai but infections of  the highly contagious ompicron variant  continued to rise  we have detected many infections after  several rounds of screening so the  situation we're facing is severe and  complicated  the city has documented more than 10 000  cases in recent weeks  most of those infected have mild  symptoms or none at all but officials  are determined to maintain what they  call a dynamic zero carving strategy  shanghai is china's main financial  center and heavy restrictions are likely  to impact the country's economic growth  the city is home to 25 million people  and is also where the headquarters of  many chinese companies are located  chinese stocks have fallen at the news  the city's shipping port remains open  but some factories including tesla the  electric car manufacturer have  temporarily suspended operations the  biggest impact is on the consumer  confidence uh the income growth has  already collapsed since the start of  2022  and  now uh the unemployment in the city  services sector and the retail sector is  quite widespread  the market confidence is quite low  authorities say food delivery supplies  are adequate and medical facilities will  remain open for those needing urgent  care  but some have complained about the poor  management of lockdown restrictions  on wednesday a shanghai nurse died from  an asthma attack after the emergency  department of her hospital was closed  for disinfection katrina you al jazeera  beijing
 

